WEBVTT

00:25:58.021 --> 00:26:00.822
The calculations may be run by computers,

00:26:00.846 --> 00:26:03.807
but they're based on
data generated by humans,

00:26:03.831 --> 00:26:06.519
and there's plenty of evidence
that computers often learn

00:26:06.543 --> 00:26:08.999
to discriminate against
marginalized groups.

00:26:09.487 --> 00:26:12.099
For example, we've seen algorithms
penalize candidates

00:26:12.123 --> 00:26:14.725
who have the word
"women's" on their resumes.

00:26:15.506 --> 00:26:17.965
Most hiring algorithms
are too much of a black box

00:26:17.989 --> 00:26:19.933
for us to even know if they're biased.

00:26:19.957 --> 00:26:22.288
Many vendors claim they're proprietary,

00:26:22.312 --> 00:26:23.940
which leaves managers in the dark

00:26:23.964 --> 00:26:26.510
about what factors
the algorithms are weighing.

00:26:26.839 --> 00:26:28.448
But some experts have pointed out

00:26:28.472 --> 00:26:30.480
that it's easier to fix a biased algorithm